WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.008 --> 00:00:22.219
Ally The new customers were the mother and little girl who'd spotted her at the park right after

2
00:00:22.279 --> 00:00:22.819
her landing.

3
00:00:22.839 --> 00:00:25.041
"I'm not an alien!"

4
00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:26.181
Ally blurted.

5
00:00:26.201 --> 00:00:28.102
"It's your word against mine!"

6
00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:30.804
The mother looked confused.

7
00:00:33.308 --> 00:00:35.809
"I mean Ally tried to laugh it off.

8
00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:37.729
"Just kidding.

9
00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.370
Beep-beep! Boop!"

10
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.310
She made a few strange sounds.

11
00:00:42.471 --> 00:00:45.031
"Okay, I'm an alien!"

12
00:00:45.772 --> 00:00:48.492
The little girl laughed at Ally's funny alien imitation.

13
00:00:50.273 --> 00:00:53.134
"See, Mommy!

14
00:00:53.154 --> 00:00:55.274
I told you she was an alien.

15
00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:59.215
Can we bring Grandpa Lloyd here so he can see her too?"

16
00:00:59.235 --> 00:01:04.014
"Come along, honey," the mother said as she led her daughter out of the diner.

17
00:01:04.034 --> 00:01:06.335
"We'll be late for Grandpa's lecture."

18
00:01:09.257 --> 00:01:13.280
They were finally gone, but Ally could still feel her heart pounding in her chest.

19
00:01:14.401 --> 00:01:18.924
She went over to the counter to refill some salt shakers, but she was so rattled, she spilled

20
00:01:19.004 --> 00:01:20.165
salt all over the place.

21
00:01:22.747 --> 00:01:24.849
She was cleaning it up when Ray called from the kitchen.

22
00:01:24.869 --> 00:01:27.651
"Ally!" He sounded mad.

23
00:01:27.671 --> 00:01:29.332
"I need to speak with you."

24
00:01:32.256 --> 00:01:32.817
"Oh no!

25
00:01:33.037 --> 00:01:33.657
What now?"

26
00:01:34.037 --> 00:01:35.398
she thought, going into the kitchen.

27
00:01:35.418 --> 00:01:41.723
"I think it's time you found a new job," Ray said sternly.

28
00:01:42.864 --> 00:01:44.445
Ally's eyes filled with tears.

29
00:01:44.465 --> 00:01:47.607
"Is it because of what the little girl said?

30
00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:50.389
I promise you, I'm not what you think, Ray.

31
00:01:50.789 --> 00:01:56.413
I mean, I am, but I was only trying to do good deeds and restore peaceful balance here!"

32
00:01:58.654 --> 00:01:59.835
Ray scratched his head.

33
00:01:59.855 --> 00:02:04.185
"What?" "Never mind.

34
00:02:04.445 --> 00:02:05.506
Why do I have to leave?"

35
00:02:05.906 --> 00:02:06.487
Ally asked.

36
00:02:06.507 --> 00:02:12.652
"I can't afford to keep the diner open any longer," Ray explained.

37
00:02:12.672 --> 00:02:14.413
"I'm shutting down."

38
00:02:15.954 --> 00:02:18.156
"But we were so busy today.

39
00:02:18.557 --> 00:02:20.158
You can't give up now, Ray!"

40
00:02:20.178 --> 00:02:24.241
"One good day isn't going to save me, Ally.

41
00:02:24.521 --> 00:02:25.883
I—" "Oh my gosh!"

42
00:02:26.303 --> 00:02:26.923
Kate cried.

43
00:02:27.944 --> 00:02:29.766
Ally and Ray raced into the dining room.

44
00:02:31.627 --> 00:02:32.328
"What's wrong?"

45
00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:33.313
Ray cried.

46
00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:35.294
Kate looked up from her phone.

47
00:02:35.314 --> 00:02:38.197
"Have you ever heard of Gourmet Greta?"

48
00:02:39.298 --> 00:02:40.559
"No," Ray said.

49
00:02:40.579 --> 00:02:43.882
"Well, she's the hottest food blogger there is.

50
00:02:44.402 --> 00:02:46.124
I follow her on all my socials.

51
00:02:46.904 --> 00:02:49.967
A review from Gourmet Greta can make or break a restaurant."

52
00:02:49.987 --> 00:02:56.032
"A big-time restaurant critic is never going to come to Sandville to review a diner," Ray said.

53
00:02:56.052 --> 00:02:59.195
"She already has!"

54
00:02:59.595 --> 00:03:00.116
Kate said.

55
00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:06.224
"Look!" She held up her comm device to show them a posting: "Ray's Diner: Out of This World

56
00:03:06.264 --> 00:03:07.445
or Crashing Comet?"

57
00:03:08.786 --> 00:03:09.627
Bethany frowned.

58
00:03:09.647 --> 00:03:10.888
"I don't get it.

59
00:03:11.508 --> 00:03:13.991
Is that a good review or a bad one?"

60
00:03:14.011 --> 00:03:18.995
"Greta likes to keep the reader guessing until the last line of her review.

61
00:03:19.395 --> 00:03:22.818
She never gives away anything in the titles," Kate said.

62
00:03:23.638 --> 00:03:25.220
Worry knitted Ray's brow.

63
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:27.342
"I don't think I want to hear this."

64
00:03:29.383 --> 00:03:30.064
Kate smiled.

65
00:03:30.604 --> 00:03:31.965
"Yes, you do."

66
00:03:32.746 --> 00:03:33.506
She read aloud.

67
00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:39.892
Ray's Diner, located near Sandville's famous UFO museum, is full of surprises.

68
00:03:40.412 --> 00:03:44.675
Though the decor is simple, there's nothing plain about the food or the service.

69
00:03:45.196 --> 00:03:47.197
Everything I ate there was delicious.

70
00:03:48.038 --> 00:03:49.740
And the service is unmatched.

71
00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:54.904
There's only one waitress, and she's sweet, funny, and always seems to have a surprise up her sleeve.

72
00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:02.662
Whether she's suggesting exactly the right dish to customers or performing entertaining tricks, she always adds to the

73
00:04:02.702 --> 00:04:07.704
fun. If you're looking for great food and hospitality, head to Ray's Diner.

74
00:04:08.204 --> 00:04:09.224
A+ rating.

75
00:04:10.804 --> 00:04:11.745
Mateo cheered.

76
00:04:11.765 --> 00:04:13.585
"You're a hit, Papi!"

77
00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:22.848
But Ally was confused.

78
00:04:23.572 --> 00:04:26.074
"I don't recall serving any restaurant critics."

79
00:04:27.134 --> 00:04:33.738
"Gourmet Greta dresses up in disguises so nobody knows she's reviewing the restaurant," Kate explained.

80
00:04:33.758 --> 00:04:39.161
"But she includes a photo in her reviews—it has hints of what she wore to the restaurant."

81
00:04:40.922 --> 00:04:42.723
Ally examined the photo in the review.

82
00:04:42.743 --> 00:04:48.466
"The hints are big eyeglasses, a cane, and a leopard-print dress.

83
00:04:49.307 --> 00:04:51.608
I served this woman three different times."

84
00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.580
"Wait, there's more."

85
00:04:59.041 --> 00:05:00.941
Bethany read from her own comm device.

86
00:05:00.961 --> 00:05:05.842
"'The only thing Ray's is missing to attract more customers is a theme.

87
00:05:06.483 --> 00:05:12.884
Ray, if you want Greta's advice, remember that you're the closest restaurant to the museum.

88
00:05:13.405 --> 00:05:17.586
So a UFO or space theme would be a perfect fit.'"

89
00:05:17.606 --> 00:05:20.006
"Awesome idea!"

90
00:05:20.547 --> 00:05:21.307
Mateo said.

91
00:05:22.047 --> 00:05:23.527
Ray lifted his eyebrows.

92
00:05:23.547 --> 00:05:29.893
"It might work "Can I help with new decorations?"

93
00:05:30.413 --> 00:05:31.154
Bethany asked.

94
00:05:32.074 --> 00:05:34.615
"Yes!" Mateo's cheeks turned red again.

95
00:05:34.635 --> 00:05:37.636
"I'll help too," Kate said.

96
00:05:37.656 --> 00:05:39.457
"I'm really good at shopping."

97
00:05:40.378 --> 00:05:42.199
"Let's get to work," Ray said.

98
00:05:44.099 --> 00:05:47.901
Ally stood back, watching as the others started planning the restaurant makeover.

99
00:05:48.982 --> 00:05:51.543
She was happy that Ray's Diner might be saved after all.

100
00:05:52.023 --> 00:05:53.704
But now she herself needed help.

101
00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.102
"If the little girl brings Dr.

102
00:05:57.182 --> 00:06:04.931
Cosmo Lloyd to the diner," Ally thought, "I'm in trouble—meteor-size trouble!"
